#static
STEP 1 — VERIFY PUBLIC IP

Inside Azure VM page check:

Public IP Address

Make sure you are opening:

http://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP

NOT:

https://

Use only:

http
STEP 2 — CHECK PORT 80

VERY IMPORTANT.

Go to:

VM → Networking

Check:

Inbound Port Rules

You should see:

Port	Status
22	Allow
80	Allow
IF PORT 80 NOT PRESENT

Click:

Add inbound port rule

Fill:

Field	Value
Destination Port	80
Protocol	TCP
Action	Allow

Click:

Add

Wait 1 minute.

Then refresh browser.

STEP 3 — TEST APACHE INSIDE VM

In terminal run:

curl localhost
EXPECTED OUTPUT

You should see HTML content or Apache page.

If yes:

Apache working correctly ✅
STEP 4 — CHECK APACHE AGAIN

Run:

sudo systemctl status apache2

Must show:

active (running)
STEP 5 — CHECK FIREWALL

Run:

sudo ufw status

If firewall active:
allow HTTP:

sudo ufw allow 80
STEP 6 — RESTART APACHE

Run:

sudo systemctl restart apache2
STEP 7 — OPEN WEBSITE AGAIN

Browser:

http://ip



echo Hello Secure File Sharing > test.txt
dir
STEP 5 — CONNECT TO VM USING SSH

Run:

ssh vijay@ip
STEP 6 — KEEP SSH WINDOW OPEN

Do NOT close it.

STEP 7 — OPEN NEW CMD WINDOW

Open another Command Prompt.

STEP 8 — TRANSFER FILE USING SCP

Run:

scp test.txt vijay@ip:/home/vijay
STEP 9 — ENTER PASSWORD

Type VM password.

(Password invisible → normal)

EXPECTED OUTPUT

You’ll see something like:

test.txt       100%

This means transfer successful ✅
STEP 10 — VERIFY INSIDE VM

Go back to SSH terminal.

Run:

ls

You should see:

test.txt

DONE ✅

STEP 11 — VIEW FILE CONTENT

### Fullstack
STEP 2 — START EXISTING VM

Go to:

Virtual Machines

Select your VM.

Click:

Start

Wait until:

Running
STEP 3 — COPY PUBLIC IP

Inside VM page:
Copy:

Public IP

Example:

20.193.145.146
STEP 4 — OPEN CMD

On Windows:
Open:

Command Prompt
STEP 5 — CONNECT USING SSH

Run:

ssh vijay@20.193.145.146

Enter password.

STEP 6 — UPDATE SYSTEM

Run:

sudo apt update
STEP 7 — INSTALL APACHE

Run:

sudo apt install apache2 -y
STEP 8 — START APACHE

Run:

sudo systemctl start apache2
STEP 9 — ENABLE APACHE

Run:

sudo systemctl enable apache2
STEP 10 — CHECK APACHE STATUS

Run:

sudo systemctl status apache2

Check:

active (running)

Press:

q

to exit.

STEP 11 — INSTALL GIT

Run:

sudo apt install git -y
STEP 12 — GO TO HOME DIRECTORY

Run:

cd ~
STEP 13 — CLONE GITHUB PROJECT

Run:

git clone https://github.com/Vijaylaxmi-30/Helpdesk-Management--Expert-System-.git
STEP 14 — CHECK PROJECT

Run:

ls

You should see:

Helpdesk-Management--Expert-System-
STEP 15 — GO INSIDE PROJECT

Run:

cd Helpdesk-Management--Expert-System-
STEP 16 — VERIFY FILES

Run:

ls

Check:

index.html

exists.

VERY IMPORTANT.

STEP 17 — REMOVE OLD WEBSITE FILES

Run:

sudo rm -rf /var/www/html/*
STEP 18 — COPY PROJECT FILES

Run:

sudo cp -r * /var/www/html/
STEP 19 — RESTART APACHE

Run:

sudo systemctl restart apache2
STEP 20 — OPEN WEBSITE

Browser:

http://20.193.145.146

Your GitHub project opens ✅

STEP 21 — STOP VM AFTER PRACTICAL

VERY IMPORTANT.

Azure Portal:

VM → Stop

Wait for:

Stopped (deallocated)

To save credits.

Run:

cat test.txt

Output:

Hello Secure File Sharing
